message: "If you use this software, please cite both the article and this archive."
title: "Weighted spatial averages with missing observations: Convergence and accuracy of delta-method variance approximations (code)"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB code and data accompanying the paper "Weighted spatial averages with
  missing observations: Convergence and accuracy of delta-method variance
  approximations". When observations are missing at random, a weighted spatial
  average is a ratio of two random quantities, and its variance is usually
  approximated by truncating a Taylor series of the ratio (the delta method).
  The code computes a two-index sequence of such approximations, the exact
  variance for uniform weights (as a single sum over the number of reporting
  sites), and the exact variance for small networks with arbitrary weights (by
  enumerating all reporting patterns). It reproduces every figure and table in
  the paper using a homogeneous benchmark, small synthetic networks, and India
  Meteorological Department (IMD) 1° gridded daily rainfall.
